  "question": {
    "text": "A circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;passes through the origin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;and has diameter&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> on the positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis. The line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;gives a chord&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></math> of a circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the circle with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;as a diameter. If the tangent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> meets the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
